<p>Unauthorized personnel boarded a vessel anchored off the east coast of the United Arab Emirates on Thursday and directed it toward Iranian territorial waters, the United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations center said. UKMTO said the incident occurred 38 nautical miles, or about 70 kilometers, northeast of Fujairah, near the southern approach to the Strait of Hormuz. Two maritime security sources said the ship was believed to be the Honduras-flagged Hui Chuan fishery research vessel.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/lujEGWPTBvRQgf_7InYy8b0xVIONVcFhj1o2pJoe8Zd_tDfB59dvSbqCJUtiGBSf5i4NhSPg3nXKXSqHY7dLqNyQ4hJNITR1NfjxyeJwltP9fa4ndHUBNG70ku44c1l3kdBbRVVs0O1PkPrwo-KWc90KGqxt2Tmr6Vm47_GBLwPhczVKJAubQyP_QaXIOgrnyymjulosVtHw_3uL3-hkRbe9PJd7yTjME_ZtYrbZWekQB6oohv3nnegbE0kf8jVP-E-y52d2rU35du08QA' alt='Vessels in the Strait of Hormuz, Musandam, Oman, May 8, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Boarding time: British maritime risk firm Vanguard said the boarding occurred at 0545 GMT on Thursday, citing reporting from the vessel’s company security officer.</li><li>Tracking update: Vanguard said contact with the Hui Chuan later broke down entirely and the ship stopped transmitting through AIS.</li><li>No immediate claim: Authorities and initial reports cited no public claim of responsibility for taking the vessel.</li><li>Other recent attacks: South Korean coverage said a Korean cargo ship had been attacked by an unidentified flying object earlier in May and that Qatar had reported a drone attack on a cargo ship arriving from Abu Dhabi.</li></ul><blockquote>From our perspective, the Strait of Hormuz is open to all commercial vessels, but they must cooperate with our naval forces - Abbas Araghchi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations: UKMTO said it was investigating and initially did not identify the vessel or who had taken control of it. (<a href='https://mynorthwest.com/world/ship-is-reported-seized-off-the-coast-of-the-u